ok   parse decodes scalars, lists, nested params and bare flags
ok   parse decodes '+' as space and percent-escapes
ok   parse of a malformed percent-escape raises QueryMalformed on every runtime
ok   decode_escapes (the loop under decode and Request.split_path) leaves '+' alone when asked
ok   decode handles runs of escapes, '+', and non-ASCII text between them
ok   decode_escapes refuses a percent sign that is not followed by two hex digits, whatever its caller checked
ok   an invalid byte sequence is QueryMalformed, not IndexError, raw or percent-encoded
ok   decode of valid percent-encoded multibyte text still works, a malformed escape keeps its own message
ok   parse of a 100-pair valid non-ASCII body still works
ok   parse_into writes into the caller's Params, later pairs over earlier ones, and parse is parse_into on a fresh one
ok   value_of answers what Params#[] answers after a parse
ok   valid_escapes? wants two hex digits after every percent sign
ok   parse of an empty string yields an empty Params
ok   split_key splits scalar, nested and list-in-nested forms
ok   split_key treats a malformed bracket as part of a plain key
ok   encode round-trips through parse
16 tests, 126 assertions, 0 failures
